f restart_game(self):\n    """Restart the game."""\n    # Instead of importing CheckersGame, create a new instance\n    # by re-initializing the existing game object\n    self.game.init()\n\n\n**Alternative better solution:**\nAdd a `reset()` method to the `CheckersGame` class in `game.py`:\n\nIn `game.py`, add to the `CheckersGame` class:\npython\ndef reset(self):\n    """Reset the game to initial state."""\n    self.init()\n\n\nThen in `gui.py`, modify `restart_game()`:\npython\ndef restart_game(self):\n    """Restart the game."""\n    self.game.reset()\n``\n\n**Additional minor issues to consider after fixing the main issue:**\n1. The move notation display (draw_move_notation()`) shows coordinates but the prompt mentions "2,1 to 3,2" format - consider making the notation more user-friendly\n2. The mandatory capture logic appears correct but should be thoroughly tested\n\nThe suggested fix ensures that all regulations are met, particularly #1 (imports work correctly), #4 (no potential bugs), and #6 (full user interaction capability).'} |
